<title>USA: PureTec exchanges preferred, common stock.</title>
<headline>PureTec exchanges preferred, common stock.</headline>
<dateline>RIDGEFIELD, N.J. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>PureTec International Corp said Monday holders of its Class A Preferred Stock had agreed to exchange the shares for common stock effective July 31, 1996.</p>
<p>PureTec, which makes plastic products such as garden hoses, said directors and officers would own 21.5 percent more stock as a result.</p>
